body:
Hi. I've discovered two issues with `message/extract` command when working with `.po` files in `MessageController::saveMessagesToPO()` method.
##### Translation files are not updated when translation messages are updated (without adding or deleting new entries)

For example. Lets assume we have a `Yii:t()` call: `Yii:t('category', 'some message')`.
We generate initial translation files with `message/extract` command. After that we want to change `Yii:t('category', 'some message')` to `Yii:t('category', 'some new message')`. After change we run `message/extract` command again, but translation files will not be updated.

I think the reason is here ([MessageController.php#L422-L425](https://github.com/yiisoft/yii2/blob/master/framework/console/controllers/MessageController.php#L422-L425)):

``` php
if (array_keys($existingMessages) == $msgs) {
    echo "Nothing new... skipped.\n";
    return self::EXIT_CODE_NORMAL;
}
```

While this is able to find difference between arrays:

``` php
if (!array_diff(array_values($msgs), array_keys($existingMessages))) {
    echo "Nothing new... skipped.\n";
    return self::EXIT_CODE_NORMAL;
}
```
##### Incorrect handling of multiple messages categories

The same code snippet  ([MessageController.php#L422-L425](https://github.com/yiisoft/yii2/blob/master/framework/console/controllers/MessageController.php#L422-L425)):

``` php
if (array_keys($existingMessages) == $msgs) {
    echo "Nothing new... skipped.\n";
    return self::EXIT_CODE_NORMAL;
}
```

has another bug in `return self::EXIT_CODE_NORMAL;`. It should not do this because it breaks work with multiple messages categories.
For example, we have three categories: `messages`, `attributes` and `general`. Lets say we updated our code and have changed `Yii:t()` calls with `messages` and `attributes` categories. Now let's see what `MessageController::saveMessagesToPO()` method will do (as there are a `foreach` at [MessageController.php#L414](https://github.com/yiisoft/yii2/blob/master/framework/console/controllers/MessageController.php#L414)):
1. It will find changed messages in `messages` category and print `Translation merged`.
2. It will find changed messages in `attributes` category and print `Translation merged`.
3. It will not find changed messages in `general` category and print `Nothing new... skipped` and will `return self::EXIT_CODE_NORMAL`.

As a result, `$poFile->save($file, $merged);` (at [MessageController.php#L472](https://github.com/yiisoft/yii2/blob/master/framework/console/controllers/MessageController.php#L472)) will never be triggered and `.po` file will not be saved.

I think usage of `continue;` command instead of `return self::EXIT_CODE_NORMAL;` should fix this issue.
